The review is concerned with the regulated entity’s claims practices by line of business for compliance
with statutes, rules and regulations and policy provisions. The areas to be considered in this kind of
review include:
a.
Time studies to measure acknowledgment, investigation and settlement times;
b.
General handling study;
c.
Total loss valuation survey;
d.
Closed without payment survey;
e.
Subrogation survey;
f.
Litigation survey;
g.
Unfair claims practices survey;
h.
Claims form review;
i.
Loss statistical reporting survey;
j.
Time study on canceled checks; and
k.
Review of other procedures, as deemed necessary.

